CineTaste — Full Product Documentation
Version: 1.0
Document Purpose:

To define all features, flows, design principles, and user experience elements of the CineTaste application.

1. Introduction
1.1 Overview

CineTaste is a personalized entertainment-tracking and recommendation platform for movies, series, animations, and anime. It helps users maintain a record of everything they watch, organize future watchlists, rate titles, receive intelligent suggestions, and explore detailed title information.

Unlike generic streaming guides or watchlist apps, CineTaste focuses on understanding the user’s taste. Using pattern analysis, moods, tags, and ratings, CineTaste recommends content tailored to each individual user. It also provides optional social features with strong privacy controls.

2. Product Vision
2.1 Mission Statement

To create the most intelligent and personal entertainment companion — one that understands a user’s unique taste and helps them discover what they will truly enjoy watching.

2.2 Target Goals

Provide a centralized space to track all entertainment consumed.

Deliver smart recommendations based on mood, taste, and activity.

Make discovery easier with clean interfaces and detailed content pages.

Offer safe, permission-based social interaction.

Maintain a premium, cinematic user experience.

3. Target Users

CineTaste is designed for:

Movie lovers

Series binge-watchers

Anime and animation fans

People who enjoy reviewing, tracking, and organizing media

Users frustrated by poor recommendations on streaming platforms

Friends who enjoy sharing what they watch (with privacy controls)

4. Core Features
4.1 MyWatch List

A central feature where users save titles they want to watch later.
Features include:

Add any movie/series/anime/animation

Custom categories (e.g., “Weekend Picks,” "Anime Queue")

Sort by genre, length, release year, or urgency

One-tap “Mark as Watched”

Sync suggestions based on pending items

4.2 History Timeline

A visual chronological timeline showing:

Titles watched

Date completed

User rating

Mood tags

Notes or reviews

Users can filter history by:

Genre

Mood

Year watched

Rating

Title type (movies/series/anime/etc.)

4.3 Smart Auto Suggestions (AI Taste Engine)

This is the intelligence behind CineTaste.
It analyzes:

Your ratings

Genres you rate highly

Directors/actors you frequently enjoy

Moods you choose

Completion habits (e.g., you finish thrillers faster than sci-fi)

Your weekly/monthly watching patterns

The engine creates:

For You Picks

Top 10 for This Week

Because You Watched…

Hidden Gems in Your Favorite Genres

Short Movies for When You’re Busy

Anime Picks Based on Your Ratings

4.4 Rating & Review System

Users can:

Rate titles from 1–5 stars

Add mood tags (funny, emotional, dark, mind-blowing, slow-burn, etc.)

Write short reviews (optional)

Edit ratings anytime

Mood and rating data heavily influence recommendations.

4.5 Title Profile Pages

Each title has a dedicated page including:

Poster and summary

Release date + runtime

Genre and mood tags

Cast and crew

Trailer (optional)

Your personal rating, notes, and tags

Similar titles generated by the AI engine

Streaming availability

Progress tracking for series (episodes/seasons completed)

4.6 Mood Recommender

A unique recommendation mode based on emotional state.
User chooses a mood such as:

Laugh

Cry

Romantic

Mind-blowing

Action

Sci-Fi Vibes

Dark/Mysterious

Feel-Good

CineTaste then filters titles using mood tags + user taste patterns.

4.7 Stats Dashboard

A visually rich analytics system showing:

Most-watched genres

Favorite directors & actors

Monthly watching trends

Best-rated content

Longest binge streak

Total hours watched

Auto-generated “Top 10 of the Year” list

This dashboard makes entertainment consumption more fun and insightful.

4.8 Multi-User System

Each user has:

Independent account

Personalized watchlists, ratings, and suggestions

Secure login

Profile customization (avatar, username, bio)

Families or friends can use CineTaste on shared devices without mixing data.

4.9 Friends & Social Mode (With Permissions)

Users can:

Add friends

Request to view friend activity

Compare ratings

See what friends love (only if allowed)

Privacy Approach

Users can choose whether others can see:

Their watchlist

Ratings

Reviews

Recent activity

Genre preferences

No data is shown until explicit permission is granted.

5. App Structure
5.1 Main Sections

Home (recommendations + quick actions)

MyWatch List

History Timeline

Explore/Search

Stats Dashboard

Friends & Social

Account Settings

6. User Experience (UX) Principles

Cinematic Feel: A dark, immersive interface inspired by movie theatres.

Minimal Clutter: Clean spacing, large posters, easy navigation.

Fast Interaction: One-click ratings, swipe to add/remove, smooth transitions.

Consistency: Repeated icon patterns, predictable layouts, strong UI hierarchy.

Privacy First: Clear permission prompts, transparent social controls.

7. Design & Color System

CineTaste uses the Cinematic Dark Palette.

Primary Color

Red — #E50914
Used for primary actions, highlights, buttons, and accents.

Secondary Color

Dark Charcoal — #221F1F
Used for card backgrounds, navigation bars, panels.

Accent Color

Off-White — #F5F5F5
Used for all readable text and icons.

Highlight Color

Deep Red — #B81D24
Used for selection indicators, active states, mood tags.

Background Color

Blackish — #121212
Used as the global background for maximum immersion.

8. Accessibility Guidelines

High contrast text (#F5F5F5 on #121212) ensures readability.

Icons and buttons must maintain a minimum hit size.

Alternative text used for posters and images.

Option to increase font size.

9. Security & Privacy
9.1 Data Protection

All profiles separated

Encrypted user authentication

Activity visible only with explicit approval

9.2 Permissions

For each friend request, user chooses what is visible.
Default visibility = Private.

10. Future Roadmap (Optional Features)
Possible Add-ons

Community groups

Shared watchlists

AI-powered “watch tonight” picker

Notification system for new recommendations

Cloud sync for multiple devices

Import/export watchlist from other platforms

Offline mode

11. Conclusion

CineTaste aims to become the go-to platform for anyone who loves watching movies, series, anime, and animations. It provides a powerful combination of tracking, discovery, personalization, and authentic user control — all wrapped within a modern, cinematic interface.

With a strong foundation, privacy-first social features, and a rich AI recommendation engine, CineTaste stands out not just as a watchlist app, but as a full entertainment companion.